{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  "extends": ["//"],
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — the same defect `deploy/airgap/turbo.json`, `tools/helm-verify/turbo.json`,
  // `packages/plugins/managed-scan/turbo.json` and `apps/server/turbo.json` each document, found HERE
  // by the M23.0 verification-pass-8 sweep that went looking for it rather than by a red test — this
  // package is the one that WROTE those other four files' shared reasoning and had never applied it
  // to itself.
  //
  // TWO of this package's own unit tests are censuses of files OUTSIDE `packages/source-census/**`,
  // and turbo hashed neither:
  //   - `golden-count-gate.test.ts` reads `docs/BUILD_AND_TEST.md`'s M23.0 bullet and the three
  //     `launch-argv.golden.test.ts` files (managed-iac/managed-scan/managed-dep) and fails the
  //     moment the documented count and the real `it(` count disagree.
  //   - `test-script-census.test.ts` runs `git ls-files` and reads EVERY tracked `package.json`
  //     (scripts) and every tracked `*.test.ts` filename, repo-wide, to assert no `test`/
  //     `test:integration` script can report success for having run nothing.
  //
  // MEASURED, not inferred (M23.0 verification pass 8): seeded a cache with `turbo run test
  // --filter=@scp/source-census`, then appended a throwaway `it(` to
  // `packages/plugins/managed-dep/src/launch-argv.golden.test.ts` (a real drift golden-count-gate
  // exists to catch) and reran the SAME command with no `--force`. It printed `>>> FULL TURBO`, 2/2
  // cached, green — the count mismatch never ran. Structurally identical to the measured
  // `@scp/plugin-managed-scan` defect (an unvetted `ARG TRIVY_IMAGE=` digest going 5/5 cached green)
  // this package's own `INTEGRATION_FLAG_ALLOWLIST` comment already names. The mutation was reverted
  // immediately after being observed.
  //
  // DELIBERATELY WIDE, for the same reason `packages/plugins/managed-scan/turbo.json` gives:
  // `test-script-census.test.ts`'s subject is "every package.json and every *.test.ts filename in
  // the repo", which is a property of the WHOLE tree, not a short list of named files — narrowing
  // this to golden-count-gate's three files would silently stop protecting the other census. Root
  // `package.json` is listed explicitly because it sits outside every `apps/**|packages/**|...` glob
  // below but is itself one of `test-script-census.test.ts`'s subjects (its own `test`/
  // `test:integration` scripts).
  "tasks": {
    "test": {
      "dependsOn": ["build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/package.json",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/docs/BUILD_AND_TEST.md",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/deploy/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/scripts/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/tools/**"
      ]
    }
  }
}
